build*/
*.profraw

opencode.json

# NOT ignored, deliberately: .opencode/agents/. Those two role prompts were
# removed from tracking and ignored here on 2026-09-07 on the premise that the
# loop regenerates them at start-up from ANTfrastructure's
# shared/agentic-loop/system-prompts/<role>.md plus this repo's
# scripts/agentic-loop/prompts/<role>-overlay.md. No such generator exists at
# the pinned submodule commit: there is no Write-AgenticOpenCodeAgentFile (or
# any other writer of .opencode/) anywhere in ANTfrastructure, and the Bash half's
# invoke_opencode goes straight to `opencode run --agent <role>`, which resolves
# .opencode/agents/<role>.md out of the checkout. Ignoring them therefore left a
# FRESH CLONE on `engine: opencode` running both roles with no role prompt at
# all - and a clone without the submodule with no way to reconstruct one.
#
# They stay tracked until a generator actually exists AND runs before the first
# opencode invocation. The drift that motivated the delete is real, but the cure
# is a gate, not a deletion: the tracked copies hold the COMPOSED
# shared-prompt + overlay text, and scripts/windows/tests/
# AgenticLoop.PromptOverlays.Tests.ps1 fails if either stops containing the
# shared role prompt or this repo's overlay verbatim. Edit the overlay.

